WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.850
Behold my end.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:13.720
What are you doing, Uncle?

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:15.570
This is far too pitiful.

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.010
Ebisugawa Soun...

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:23.390
embarks now for the realm of the dead.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:37.760
<b>The Late Ebisugawa Soun</b>

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:37.760
<b>Mourning</b>

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:39.790
Both Sou-san and Ebisugawa-san
have departed for the next world.

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:41.460
Mother...

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:47.380
Ebisugawa-san volunteered to marry
into the Ebisugawa family himself.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.780
Originally, your grandfather

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:56.230
wanted to do something
about the feud with the Ebisugawas.

00:00:56.610 --> 00:01:00.620
So he went to make peace with them, but...

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:06.060
But apparently, Soun had already
been talking with the Ebisugawa family.

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:10.100
He joined the Ebisugawas
to bring peace between the families.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:13.410
Why did something like this have to happen?

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:15.750
I see.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.130
So Mother doesn't understand.

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:20.620
How sad.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:23.910
I've become rather sick of it all.

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:26.730
Tanuki are truly foolish creatures.

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:28.480
Fools!

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:36.080
"Nasebanaru" to hito wa yuuga

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:36.080
People say, "Where there's 
a will, there's a way"

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:39.580
Narugamama naseba ii

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:39.580
But things can just be how they'll be

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:52.180
Nagareru kawa ukabu kobune

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:52.180
A small boat floats along the river

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:56.130
Doko ni yukuno darouka

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:56.130
I wonder where it's going

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:01.320
Ikisaki nado yosou dekinu

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:01.320
I can't even guess its destination

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:05.600
Sorega omoshiroki koto

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:05.600
But that's why it's so fun

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:14.730
Kokorozashi wa takaku mokuhyou wa hikuku

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:14.730
My intentions are high, but my goals are low

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:19.800
Aho wo mazerya kekka

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:19.800
When foolishness gets mixed in

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:26.830
Yukai ni nareru

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:26.830
Everything will be merry

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:33.560
Narugamama ni sawagu mama ni

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:33.560
As things will be, as chaotic as they will be

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:38.260
Toraburu suramo nenryou sa

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:38.260
Even troubles become fuel

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:42.680
Namikaze tatanai jinsei wa

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:42.680
A life lived without any strife

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:47.220
Chotto bakkari tsumaranai

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:47.220
Can be a bit boring

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:51.960
Okiraku ni gokuraku ni

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:51.960
Carefree and blissfully

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:56.470
Kaze ni makasete ikou

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:56.470
Let's let the wind lead us

00:02:56.470 --> 00:03:00.950
Kyou mo bakashite ikou

00:02:56.470 --> 00:03:00.950
Let's go trick everyone again today

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.950
<b>Episode Eight
Ebisugawa Kaisei's Secret</b>

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.950
<b>Today's Special: Omelet Rice
(with salad and coffee)
980 yen</b>

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:10.540
Oh, it's just you, Yasaburo-chan?

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:13.950
You're such a slacker.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:17.840
On days when the weather's this bad,
you have to protect your behind.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.100
You're far too worried about
your behind, Yasaburo-chan.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.970
It's like a neurosis.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:26.790
Is it trauma from the mushrooms?

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:31.850
I felt pretty bad, considering even Kinkaku
and Ginkaku were laughing at you two.

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:35.190
You were crying your eyes out.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:37.020
Ha! Ha!

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:39.780
Your tail's in plain sight!

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:42.110
I wasn't crying my eyes out!

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:44.530
I'm just joking.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:47.490
You were always a little
tanuki who never cried.

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:52.070
I wonder what's taking Yaichiro-san so long.

00:03:55.610 --> 00:04:00.050
A tanuki playing shogi on a rainy day
is rather handsome, don't you think?

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:12.810
Kureichiro-san from the Ebisugawa family...

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:16.720
He's apparently been chanting sutras
at his father's side this whole time.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:19.600
Well, I guess he is a monk.

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:24.200
It must be hard for Kaisei-chan
to run the factory on her own.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:28.390
And I'm sure her two absolutely
idiotic brothers aren't helping.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:34.120
Oh? Did you just hear some rumbling?

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:43.890
Mother!

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:49.010
I was so frightened!
That was far too close for comfort!

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:53.990
Peeksies.

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:56.830
Oh, Gyokuran.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:58.060
Good evening.

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:04.150
I'm sorry. Thunder and lightning
always undo my transformation.

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:06.950
For me, it's the tofu seller's trumpet.

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:09.330
It always makes me feel uneasy.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:13.660
You're all so cowardly.
I don't have a single weakness.

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:15.560
Oh, really?

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:16.470
Oh?

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:23.860
Yajiro-niisan!

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:39.560
Ah, we've got a full house.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:41.720
Even Gyokuran's here.

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:46.450
Good grief. I'm not there yet.
Seeing Mother made me lose my transformation.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.860
I'm still impressed.

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:51.030
Well done, practicing that much.

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:55.820
I'm so happy to have you home, Yajiro.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:01.630
Who's there?

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:12.550
<b>Respectfully Yours</b>

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:10.970
I had hoped to find my father
and bring him here.

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:15.430
However, my Father has passed on.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:17.200
Kureichiro?

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:19.560
A million apologies would not be enough

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:22.060
to atone for my father's sins.

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:23.710
However,

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:28.380
I hope that you can show mercy on the
foolish children of the Ebisugawa family,

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:32.880
and that the Ebisugawas and Shimogawas
can become good friends.

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:37.250
I humbly ask for your support.

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:43.720
Please, I beg of you to pull out
the fur from our foolish behinds!

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:45.350
As much as you'd like!

00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:46.960
Respectfully yours!

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:50.750
Kureichiro, please lower your behind
and raise your head.

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:52.740
Please! Don't hold back!

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:54.050
Bring it on!

00:06:55.960 --> 00:07:00.970
Kureichiro, I can never forgive my uncle
for what he has done.

00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:05.820
But what good would come
of pulling out the fur from your behinds?

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:10.600
Our father's fur has returned to Heaven,
and so has our uncle's.

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:15.540
What's important is how we're
going to live from now on.

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:17.080
"How we're going to live"?

00:07:17.510 --> 00:07:20.430
Will we live together in peace or in feud?

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:26.340
I do not want the feud to continue.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:29.200
Then let us end the feud today.

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:30.760
We are all tanuki.

00:07:31.270 --> 00:07:32.720
Let us live together in peace.

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:52.420
Shimogamo Yasaburo has arrived.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:56.500
Okay, all done.

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:01.340
Oh, it's Yasaburo.

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:05.630
Well then, Master, I will be
taking my leave for the night.

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:08.850
What? But the night is still young.

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:10.940
Don't say such lonely things.

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:14.800
I have a date with a gentleman
at Kiyomizu-dera tonight.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:15.970
A date?!

00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:19.390
Please don't get too jealous.

00:08:20.950 --> 00:08:22.930
Could it be with the Nidaime?

00:08:22.930 --> 00:08:28.840
He is a vile womanizer
who's as slimy as rotten snot.

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:32.740
He didn't happen to sweet-talk
my sweet, innocent Benten, did he?

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:34.730
I'm going to Kiyomizu.

00:08:34.730 --> 00:08:35.860
Come with me.

00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:44.640
Look at all these fools.

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:47.630
At this rate, I'll never find Benten.

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:50.620
I'm pretty sure that
Benten-sama will stand out well.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:56.350
Sensei, just stay here
and enjoy some amazake.

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:58.890
I'll go look for her.

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:13.030
She really does stand out.

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:15.570
See? Over there.

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:18.680
That truly is ugly.

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:21.510
Oh? It looks like a candle and is adorable.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:27.460
Whenever I feel lonely,
I always sit atop that tower.

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:30.400
Then I start to feel better gradually.

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:35.840
So that creepy thing apparently
is good for something.

00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:39.070
You say that in such a cynical way.

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:40.960
You're just like Master.

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:43.250
That sounds rather insulting.

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:46.310
Because I said it to be insulting.

00:09:51.170 --> 00:09:53.520
You should just give up, miss.

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:56.170
This is a waste of time and effort.

00:09:56.640 --> 00:09:58.280
I guess we should.

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:02.780
What's that?

00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:06.390
I made it connecting Master's hair together.

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:09.540
I thought I would strangle
you to death with it.

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:13.130
Please, go ahead and try.

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:17.340
You're so boring.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:21.150
Thank you for spending time with me tonight.

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:23.270
I thank you from the bottom of my heart.

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:28.390
I'd rather spend time with you
than have you try to kill me in my sleep.

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:29.940
Like you're so great.

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:32.360
Of course. I am great.

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:34.960
Greater than you, in any case, miss.

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:39.340
I highly recommend
that you stop becoming a tengu.

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:41.740
There is nothing in that future for you.

00:10:42.270 --> 00:10:45.140
Then what do you suggest I do?

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:47.720
There are many other paths you could take.

00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:50.520
You act as though you know me.

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:53.750
I'm just trying to give you
some sincere advice.

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:57.130
If you've fallen for me,
why don't you just say so?

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:59.700
Please stop saying such foolish things.

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:02.100
If I were going to take your advice,

00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:04.600
I'd be better off listening to a tanuki.

00:11:08.010 --> 00:11:10.020
You're so indecisive.

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:14.540
Why did you come back?

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:16.530
To this country and to this city?

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:36.970
Master,

00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:40.090
what are you doing in a place like this?

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:43.430
Benten?

00:11:43.670 --> 00:11:45.240
You'll catch a cold.

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:47.400
Let's head home.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:56.940
<b>Rokudochinnoji Temple</b>

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:56.940
<b>Kiyomizu-dera</b>

00:12:03.520 --> 00:12:07.570
Apparently, Kureichiro gave 
Yashiro a new laboratory,

00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:09.280
so I'm going to have a look.

00:12:09.280 --> 00:12:10.730
Oh, sounds good.

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:12.560
I wanna see it, too.

00:12:14.470 --> 00:12:17.590
You've been taking
good care of Yashiro. Thank you.

00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:20.590
Oh, not at all. The pleasure's all mine.

00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:24.710
Yashiro-kun's taught me so much.

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:37.490
Are you planning on making
an android or something?

00:12:38.210 --> 00:12:40.350
Isn't this laboratory wonderful?

00:12:40.350 --> 00:12:43.280
Kureichiro-san lets me do
whatever I want in here.

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:46.750
This is all equipment that was
gathering dust in the shed.

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:50.270
We're glad that they can be of some use.

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:52.370
Have you had any electrical shocks?

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:55.280
I feel some prickles sometimes,

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:57.250
but that actually perks me up.

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:01.840
Here.

00:13:03.150 --> 00:13:04.200
What is this?

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:05.840
It's a prototype.

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:08.200
I just brewed it up.

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:18.620
This is...

00:13:19.010 --> 00:13:21.780
I'm not sure what to say.
It has a lot of depth?

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:24.650
It has its own unique, pungent aroma.

00:13:24.850 --> 00:13:27.540
In other words, it tastes awful.

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:34.830
So there is a problem with the discharger.

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:42.000
Kureichiro, please continue
to look after Yashiro.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:57.020
There's something that
I want to talk to you about.

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:57.840
Oh?

00:13:57.840 --> 00:14:01.230
You want some help from your
extremely capable brother?

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:03.310
I wouldn't really call it "help."

00:14:03.310 --> 00:14:05.500
Actually, I guess it is.

00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:09.000
However, it's a rather sensitive subject.

00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:12.450
I'm not very good
when it comes to things like this,

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:16.440
so I have no idea how I should proceed.

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:21.210
But it's a conversation that
I need to have with you, so I shall.

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:23.170
Could you just get to the point?

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:26.420
I'm about to get to it! Don't rush me!

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:33.890
Could you reinstate
your engagement with Kaisei?

00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:38.390
Where the heck did that come from?

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:42.260
Of course, we'll talk to
Kaisei and Kureichiro first, but...

00:14:42.260 --> 00:14:43.650
I refuse.

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:47.910
You haven't even had your own wedding,
and you're marrying your little brother off?

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:49.240
You're trying way too hard.

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:54.440
And a tanuki like you needs to
find a wife and settle down quick.

00:14:54.440 --> 00:14:57.290
I can just see you falling into a hot pot.

00:14:57.460 --> 00:15:01.120
So, you're trying to get Kaisei to watch me?

00:15:01.120 --> 00:15:05.450
I'm telling you that you need
to have something to protect.

00:15:05.450 --> 00:15:09.130
I'm sure it's great for you
that we've worked things out

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:11.130
with the Ebisugawas.

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:13.880
But I'm not marrying
that foul-mouthed weirdo

00:15:13.880 --> 00:15:17.270
who won't even show me what she looks like.

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:19.350
And what about Yajiro-niisan?

00:15:21.280 --> 00:15:22.460
Yasaburo...

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:25.360
This is Yajiro's idea.

00:15:28.270 --> 00:15:32.860
Yajiro-niisan's planning
to leave Kyoto, isn't he?

00:15:35.400 --> 00:15:37.580
I think we should let him go.

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:40.160
I'm definitely against that!

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:42.550
He has his own path to follow.

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:45.790
I never knew that you
were such a cold tanuki!

00:15:45.970 --> 00:15:48.520
And you have your own path, as well.

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:51.760
I'm thinking about the future
of the Shimogamo family.

00:15:52.060 --> 00:15:54.180
Father is gone.

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:58.700
If I don't think about all of you, who will?

00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:02.520
I never asked you to take Father's place!

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:04.200
You'll never be able to!

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:06.490
You're pompous for thinking that you could!

00:16:18.130 --> 00:16:19.240
I see.

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:21.140
You're right.

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:26.840
<b>Draft Beer</b>

00:16:36.350 --> 00:16:38.400
Hey, Nii-san.

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:39.560
You alive?

00:16:40.710 --> 00:16:42.330
Is that you, Yasaburo?

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:44.970
I thought you'd show up eventually.

00:16:45.670 --> 00:16:50.320
All the furniture a frog needs
fits perfectly in a handkerchief.

00:16:50.870 --> 00:16:53.610
So, you're really going to leave.

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:57.140
I know what you want to say.

00:16:57.930 --> 00:16:59.770
You're against this, right?

00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:03.740
You still can't transform properly.

00:17:04.770 --> 00:17:06.910
I'll work it out.

00:17:06.910 --> 00:17:08.820
I have Grandma's medicine, too.

00:17:09.480 --> 00:17:11.210
You'll make Mother sad.

00:17:11.700 --> 00:17:14.030
You hit me where it hurts.

00:17:14.670 --> 00:17:17.220
But I'll definitely be back.

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:19.180
Yasaburo...

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:22.760
Do you believe in the red fur of fate?

00:17:22.760 --> 00:17:23.760
Well...

00:17:24.280 --> 00:17:25.320
I don't know.

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:29.700
There are two tanuki who I know very well,

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:34.030
<b>Shimogamo Yajiro-sama, 
Wishing you a successful comeback
Ebisugawa Kaisei</b>

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:33.730
and they are completely rolled up
in the red fur of fate.

00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:37.270
It's rather strange, actually.

00:17:37.270 --> 00:17:40.300
From the outside, it's completely obvious,

00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:44.040
but they have no idea whatsoever.

00:17:44.650 --> 00:17:47.330
It's so pure and innocent.

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:50.130
It's enough to make a green frog turn red.

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:54.500
Please don't go, Nii-san.

00:17:55.790 --> 00:17:59.360
I can't coddle you forever, Yasaburo.

00:17:59.820 --> 00:18:03.810
And Yaichiro can't coddle us forever, either.

00:18:11.560 --> 00:18:13.690
It's already been a week.

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:17.700
That's a long time to run off
into the mountains to sulk.

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:21.200
I was thinking we could just let him be...

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:25.310
But he's making his family worry this much.

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:26.940
He's such a child!

00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:35.190
I have a good idea.

00:18:35.190 --> 00:18:36.590
Will you leave this to me?

00:18:37.010 --> 00:18:40.010
<b>Tanukidanisan Fudo-in Temple</b>

00:18:43.860 --> 00:18:46.470
Do you believe in the red fur of fate?

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:48.670
Suppose I did.

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:51.640
Why do I have to get
the short end of the stick?

00:18:54.160 --> 00:18:57.530
There you are, you stupid Yasaburo.

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:02.030
What are you doing here?

00:19:02.030 --> 00:19:05.320
I came to pick you up, you blockhead.

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:10.040
Not only did you make your family worry,
you made Gyokuran-sensei worry.

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:13.000
You have no sense of
responsibility as a tanuki!

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:15.300
What are you, a baby?

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:18.120
Yeah, I'm a baby.

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:19.920
Just leave me alone.

00:19:19.920 --> 00:19:21.680
See? You're being all mopey.

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:23.090
Talk about a pain!

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:25.840
I didn't ask you to come pick me up.

00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:28.470
There are times I want
to think alone, you know!

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:32.730
Hmph. And what could you think about
with that empty pepper-sized head of yours?

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:34.630
Just shut up already.

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:36.550
I'll pull out the fur from your behind!

00:19:36.550 --> 00:19:39.030
I'd like to see you try!

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:41.660
I'm not talking to you anymore.

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:43.820
Fine, I won't talk to you, either.

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:44.570
Fine!

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:46.030
Fine!

00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:53.750
I'm just talking to myself here,

00:19:54.430 --> 00:19:57.760
but I decline reinstating our engagement.

00:19:58.240 --> 00:20:02.630
I'm talking to myself, too,
but I wouldn't have it any other way.

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:05.420
It's great that we can
finally agree on something.

00:20:05.420 --> 00:20:08.140
I already have two idiots to take care of.

00:20:08.530 --> 00:20:11.350
I wouldn't be able to handle a third.

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:14.880
Yeah, and I flat-out decline, as well.

00:20:14.880 --> 00:20:19.290
What kind of tanuki would ever want
to get married to you?

00:20:19.290 --> 00:20:21.360
That tanuki would be a weirdo.

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:22.570
Oh, I see.

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:25.200
You're contrary, foul-mouthed,

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:27.420
and you haven't shown
yourself to me in years.

00:20:27.420 --> 00:20:28.700
You make no sense!

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:31.830
Yeah, yeah, I'm sure
it makes absolutely no sense.

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:36.960
I'd be happier marrying
a pickling stone than you!

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:42.800
If you're marrying a pickling stone,
then I'm marrying Hesoishi-sama!

00:20:43.220 --> 00:20:45.900
Hesoishi-sama wouldn't
fight with my brothers,

00:20:45.900 --> 00:20:49.440
or hang out with people
who eat tanuki hot pot.

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:52.980
Or fall in love with
half-ass tengu like Benten.

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:55.610
Why are you crying?

00:20:55.610 --> 00:20:57.570
Of course I'm not crying!

00:20:57.570 --> 00:20:58.980
Er, but...

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:02.450
If you want to see me so badly,
then I'll let you.

00:21:02.450 --> 00:21:03.550
Once you see me,

00:21:03.550 --> 00:21:06.660
you'll know exactly why
we could never be betrothed!

00:21:25.020 --> 00:21:26.810
I told you so!

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:28.960
If you see me,

00:21:28.960 --> 00:21:31.470
your transformation comes undone!

00:21:33.030 --> 00:21:38.250
<i>Ebisugawa Kaisei stopped showing herself
in front of me a very long time ago.</i>

00:21:39.390 --> 00:21:42.350
<i>Feeling any sense of fate
with a female tanuki</i>

00:21:42.350 --> 00:21:45.490
<i>who spews insults whenever she
opens her mouth is impossible.</i>

00:21:46.830 --> 00:21:51.280
<i>What's more, is it possible to take
someone as a wife when the sight of her</i>

00:21:51.280 --> 00:21:53.290
<i>makes your transformation come undone?</i>

00:21:54.140 --> 00:21:55.000
<i>No...</i>

00:21:56.310 --> 00:21:57.430
<i>That's not possible.</i>

00:22:04.610 --> 00:22:09.230
Tsuki wo medetewa toki ni wa nusunde

00:22:04.610 --> 00:22:09.230
While gazing lovingly at the 
moon, at times, she steals it

00:22:09.230 --> 00:22:14.100
Kimagure na kanojo wa ah

00:22:09.230 --> 00:22:14.100
Whimsical as she may be, ah

00:22:14.100 --> 00:22:18.580
Kawabe de hitori hoho ni namida

00:22:14.100 --> 00:22:18.580
As she stands by the riverside 
alone, secretly her tears

00:22:18.580 --> 00:22:22.890
Utsukushiku tayutau

00:22:18.580 --> 00:22:22.890
Quiver beautifully upon her cheeks

00:22:22.890 --> 00:22:34.700
Boku no te tori nagara 
kokoro wa dokoka ni ukabu

00:22:22.890 --> 00:22:34.700
She takes my hand, as her 
heart floats away somewhere

00:22:34.700 --> 00:22:39.190
Kasaneta te ni wa mada nukumori

00:22:34.700 --> 00:22:39.190
I still feel that warmth from her held hand

00:22:39.190 --> 00:22:43.590
Setsunai yume no sono ato saki

00:22:39.190 --> 00:22:43.590
Somewhere beyond this sentimental dream

00:22:43.590 --> 00:22:53.180
Demo kimi no me wa harukana 
mirai wo miteitane

00:22:43.590 --> 00:22:53.180
But you were already looking 
far into the future

00:22:53.180 --> 00:22:57.870
Zutto zutto oikaketayo

00:22:53.180 --> 00:22:57.870
I always chased after you

00:22:57.870 --> 00:23:02.230
Kimi ga kizutsuku toki mo

00:22:57.870 --> 00:23:02.230
Even when you were hurt

00:23:02.230 --> 00:23:11.640
Sotto mabuta ni yakitsuita kimi no sugata ni

00:23:02.230 --> 00:23:11.640
The vision of you that's 
softly imprinted on my eyes

00:23:11.640 --> 00:23:16.520
Ima mata tooku e to ah

00:23:11.640 --> 00:23:16.520
Once again, you fly far away, ah

00:23:16.520 --> 00:23:28.900
Tondeiku kimi wa hora Kanata no hito

00:23:16.520 --> 00:23:28.900
You are a person far beyond

00:23:30.940 --> 00:23:34.010
Akadama-sensei's selfishness is unbearable!

00:23:34.010 --> 00:23:36.790
What should I do?

00:23:36.790 --> 00:23:40.400
I know! Yasaburo, you deal with it!

00:23:37.350 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Episode Nine
The Various Nidaime</b>
